<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23060" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-expĕdītus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>not free.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Entangled</i>, <i>confused</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sicut pugna inexpeditior in angustiis, ita
					caedes atrocior fuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					24, 16, 3</span></i>
			 (al. impeditior).— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Not ready</i>, <i>not quick</i> at
			any thing (postclass.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Of persons: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in rebus obeundis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 7, 247</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Of
			things, <i>not easy</i>, <i>difficult</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inexpeditissimum est traducere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 5, 182</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>